{
  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "PancakeHunny",
  "name": "HunnyMinter mintFor sizes the reward from its own token balance",
  "summary": "HunnyMinter.mintFor(flip, withdrawalFee, performanceFee, to, ...) pulls the fee from the calling vault but then converts the minter's whole balance of the flip token (IBEP20(flip).balanceOf(address(this))) into HUNNY-BNB LP and mints HUNNY on that value, so tokens donated to the minter just before a vault's getReward count as performance fee. The attacker staked dust in CakeFlipVault 0x12180bb3 from helper contracts; in the anchor its contract 0x3863bdec flash-borrowed 6 WBNB, bought 125.17 CAKE, and twice sent 62.59 CAKE to the minter and called getReward from a helper, which minted 9,868 and 9,651 HUNNY that it sold into the HUNNY/WBNB pair for 5.65 and 5.50 WBNB. It repeated this in 99 more transactions through 0x3863bdec and 0xb9b0090a.",
